Subject: [PATCH 5/7] usb: usbip: bind exported devices as host class instances
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The USB/IP server looks up a device in the host support's device list
when a client imports it, and is not notified when the device is
disconnected. The device list also offers hubs, and a device that is
already exported can be imported again.

Make each device context a host class instance. The host support binds
it to a device when the device is configured, and calls its removal
handler when the device is disconnected, which clears the device pointer
with the context lock held. The submit path holds the lock until the
transfer is queued, and transfers are dequeued through the controller,
as the device may be gone. Only devices bound to a context are listed
and can be imported, hubs are left to the hub class, and an exported
device cannot be imported again.

The device list entry is filled with the lock held and sent without it,
so that a client that does not read cannot block the removal of a
device.

Assisted-by: Claude:opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Cabé <benjamin@zephyrproject.org>
